	"commit": "68ec5ca",
	"summary": "The parser and evaluator from 1.17x C++ to 1.05x with clang and from 1.08x to 0.92x with g++: Formatter appends in place and writes decimal digits without a hardware division (T-0217), and each statement's tree, in the region of its pass, is no longer dropped node by node (T-0218). With g++ every program is faster, since g++ now inlines Dazzle's functions as readily as ones declared inline (T-0190): the word count from 1.01x to 0.85x, A* search from 0.89x to 0.84x. A* search with clang moved from 0.77x to 0.80x when it took up std's BinaryHeap (T-0175). A release build from clean falls from 1.05-1.24 s to 0.53-0.81 s, and a debug rebuild after a one-line change takes 0.19-0.25 s, against 0.27-0.47 s for C++. Loops over a List now run as fast as over a slice (T-0214, T-0215), which none of these three programs has in its hot path.",
